Done on design/v1 after dc83a2b. Decisions (per user): network causes get their own codes, every auth problem is one code (auth_failed) so nothing is given away, a wrong URL is remote_not_found, offline is the fallback. Classification is substring matching on lowercased stderr with LC_ALL=C, auth checked first (Permission denied and Repository not found both come with "Could not read from remote repository"). Gotcha: newer curl says "Could not connect to server" for a refused connection, not "Connection refused"; both match. Untested against a real network: only localhost and the table of wordings.